This product bundles / depends on the following third-party components.
All are OSI-approved or open-weight and run fully on-prem (no external API at runtime).

== Runtime frameworks / libraries ==
- @airmcp-dev/core (air MCP server framework)   — Apache-2.0 — CodePedia Labs / 리원에이스
    https://github.com/airmcp-dev/air
- @modelcontextprotocol/sdk                      — MIT       (transitive via air)
- zod                                            — MIT       (transitive via air)
- TypeScript                                     — Apache-2.0 — Microsoft
    https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript
    빌드 전용(런타임에 포함되지 않는다). Apache-2.0 이라 귀속을 함께 적는다.
- pg (node-postgres)                             — MIT       — https://github.com/brianc/node-postgres

== Data substrate ==
- PostgreSQL 16                                  — PostgreSQL License (permissive, BSD-like)
- pgvector                                       — PostgreSQL License — https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector

== Models (open weights, on-prem via Ollama) ==
- Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct                            — Apache-2.0 — Alibaba Cloud
    Used for NL2SQL and final answer generation. See docs/model-cards/qwen2.5-coder-7b.md
- BGE-M3                                          — MIT        — BAAI
    Used for document/query embeddings (vector(1024)). See docs/model-cards/bge-m3.md

== Benchmark / evaluation datasets ==
- Internal contest-grade benchmark (eval/internal/*) — authored for this project,
    Apache-2.0, with generator + seed + gold SQL + raw predictions published in-repo.
- Sponsor dataset (used, not redistributed): companyx-dataset-v1.0, distributed by
    Liwonace for this contest only. Fetched by scripts/fetch-companyx-dataset.sh with a
    SHA-256 check; provenance in datasets/MANIFEST.md. No copy ships in this repository.
- External calibration (used, not redistributed): BIRD Mini-Dev (CC BY-SA 4.0).
    Downloaded locally to eval/external/ for the cross-domain calibration number in
    docs/report.md; that path is git-ignored, so this repository ships no copy of it.
    Spider (Apache-2.0) and WikiSQL (BSD-3-Clause) were considered but not used.

